cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the software version or commit you used."
title: "dx_chat_entropy: Clinical reasoning entropy and likelihood-ratio workflows"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Locke"
    given-names: "Brian W."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3588-5238"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-02-24"
abstract: >-
  Python research software for estimating, auditing, and comparing likelihood
  ratios in clinical diagnostic-reasoning workflows, including transcript-based
  assessment extraction, pairwise differential-diagnosis LR estimation, and
  one-vs-rest LR estimation with Bayes-coherent projection.
keywords:
  - "clinical reasoning"
  - "diagnostic reasoning"
  - "likelihood ratios"
  - "large language models"
  - "medical education"
  - "Bayesian reasoning"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/reblocke/dx_chat_entropy"
url: "https://github.com/reblocke/dx_chat_entropy"
